.9803,"playId":"401866465371","tiePercentage":0}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"3980","guid":"6f745f16-c96a-39c8-99ba-5c3bbd903ef8","fullName":"Waldo Stadium","address":{"city":"Kalamazoo","state":"MI","zipCode":"49008","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/college-football/day/interior/3980.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":10978},"article":{"headline":"Western Michigan builds big lead early, holds off Eastern Michigan 34-27","description":"— Jalen Buckley ran for 140 yards and two touchdowns, including a 72-yarder on the first play from scrimmage, to lead Western Michigan to a 34-27 victory over Eastern Michigan on Tuesday night.","story":"KALAMAZOO, Mich. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5085006/jalen-buckley\" target=\"_new\">Jalen Buckley</a> ran for 140 yards and two touchdowns, including a 72-yarder on the first play from scrimmage, to lead Western Michigan to a 34-27 victory over Eastern Michigan on Tuesday night. \n\n\r\n              Western Michigan (8-3, 6-1 Mid-American Conference) has won four straight games against Eastern Michigan (4-7, 3-4). \n\n\r\n              Buckley added a short-yardage touchdown run to cap an 11-play, 93-yard drive that stretched the Western Michigan lead to 14-0 midway through the first quarter. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4917858/cole-cabana\" target=\"_new\">Cole Cabana</a>'s 2-yard scoring run for Western Michigan with 40 seconds left in the second quarter made it 24-7. On the ensuing series, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4869526/dillon-moore\" target=\"_new\">Dillon Moore</a> intercepted a <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5144207/jace-stuckey\" target=\"_new\">Jace Stuckey</a> pass and ran 50 yards into the end zone to stretch the Broncos' lead to 31-7 at halftime. \n\n\r\n              In the third quarter, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5222594/amareon-blue\" target=\"_new\">Amareon Blue</a> ran for a 41-yard touchdown, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5094040/brogan-mccaughey\" target=\"_new\">Brogan McCaughey</a> tossed a 1-yard TD pass to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4582073/joshua-long\" target=\"_new\">Joshua Long</a> that pulled Eastern Michigan to 31-20. Blue's 1-yard run ended the scoring with 7:36 to play. \n\n\r\n              On their final drive, McCaughey led the Spartans to the Western Michigan 22, but he was sacked on fourth-and-7 with 30 seconds left. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5074245/broc-lowry\" target=\"_new\">Broc Lowry</a> completed 12 of 18 passes for 106 yards, and he added 57 yards on the ground for Western Michigan, which has won six of its last seven games. \n\n\r\n              McCaughey was 12-of-16 passing for 135 yards for the Spartans. Blue had 160 yards on 27 carries. He also had a 7-yard scoring run in the first quarter. \n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Eastern Michigan: concludes its regular season at home against Kent State on Tuesday. \n\n\r\n              Western Michigan: at home against Miami (Ohio) in a regular-season finale on Tuesday. \n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>, visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-18T15:12:55Z"}}